#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:19
msgid "Vibration Alert System with IFTTT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:28
msgid "This project sets up a vibration detection system using an Arduino board (Uno R4 or R3) with an ESP8266 module and a vibration sensor (SW-420). When a vibration is detected, the system sends an HTTP request to an IFTTT server, potentially triggering various actions such as sending a notification or an email."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_esp01/04-iot_Vibration_alert_system.rst:30
msgid "To avoid excessive alerts within a short timeframe, the system has been programmed to send these HTTP requests at a minimum interval of 2 minutes (120000 milliseconds). This interval could be adjusted based on the user's needs."
msgstr ""

